{=============================================================================
  Air cooled in a vertical piston-cylinder with stops
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0214
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A frictionless piston with stops closes a vertical cylinder of air. Cooling
  at constant pressure brings the piston to the stops; further cooling is at
  constant volume. The model gives the air temperature at the stops and the
  pressure after cooling to the final temperature, plus the same two results
  from the ideal-gas law. Teaching exercise, ULiège MECA0002, thermodynamique
  appliquée, repetition 2 (2022-2023).

  Inputs : A_p, T_0, p_0, h_0, T_2
  Outputs: T_1, p_2, T_1_gp, p_2_gp
  Units  : SI - temperatures in K, pressures in Pa, energies in J
           (property calls receive °C)
  Source : ULiège MECA0002, R2_E4_2022.EES; the file names no author - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Problem"
"A vertical cylinder closed by a frictionless piston fitted with stops contains air. The piston area is 0.2 m^2. The air is initially at 200 kPa and 500 C. It is then cooled by heat transfer to the surroundings, as in the original."
"a. What is the temperature of the air in the cylinder when the piston reaches the stops, as in the original."
"b. If cooling continues until the temperature reaches 20 C, what is the pressure inside the cylinder in that final state, as in the original."

"!Data"
A_p = 0.2 [m^2]                                          "piston area [m^2]"
T_0 = 500 [K]+273.15 [K]                                 "initial temperature [K]; 500 C written as 500 K + 273.15 K, as stored"
p_0 = 200e3 [Pa]                                         "initial pressure [Pa], 200 kPa in the original"
h_0 = 2 [m]                                              "initial piston height [m]"
T_2 = 20 [K]+273.15 [K]                                  "final temperature [K]; 20 C written as 20 K + 273.15 K, as stored"

"!Temperature when the piston reaches the stops"
"Constant pressure and fixed mass, as in the original."
Vol_0 = A_p*h_0                                          "initial volume [m^3]"
v_air = volume(Air, T=T_0-273.15, P=p_0)                "initial specific volume [m^3/kg]; the call takes °C and T_0 is in K"
m_air = Vol_0/v_air                                      "mass of air [kg]"

h_1 = h_0/2                                              "piston height at the stops [m], half the initial height, as written"
Vol_1 = A_p*h_1                                          "volume at the stops [m^3]"
v_1 = Vol_1/m_air                                        "specific volume at the stops [m^3/kg]"
T_1 = temperature(Air, P=p_0, V=v_1)+273.15              "temperature at the stops [K]; temperature() returns °C"

"!Further cooling at constant volume"
"Volume and mass are unchanged, so the specific volume is unchanged, as in the original."
p_2 = pressure(Air, T=T_2-273.15, V=v_1)                "pressure after cooling to T_2 [Pa]; the call takes °C and T_2 is in K"

"!Ideal-gas check"
"Isobaric process: the ratio T/V is unchanged. Use kelvin in the ideal-gas law, as in the original."
iso_p = (T_0)/Vol_0                                      "T/V along the isobar [K/m^3]"
T_1_gp = iso_p*Vol_1                                     "temperature at the stops from the ideal-gas law [K]"

"Isochoric process: the ratio T/P is unchanged, as in the original."
iso_v = (T_1_gp)/p_0                                     "T/P along the isochore [K/Pa]; p_0 is in Pa (kPa in the original)"
p_2_gp = (T_2)/iso_v                                     "pressure after cooling from the ideal-gas law [Pa]"
